   "check": "C2 THE z1-DEGREES ARE THE LANDED TOTAL DEGREES.  6, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16 -- this is the same table the transport note records as the generators' top weights, so the structure is a property of the landed objects and not of a re-normalization",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "C3 Bbar IS THE MINIMAL-DEGREE z1-MONIC GENERATOR, WITH CONSTANT 1889568/244140625.  Hence QQ[z1,z2,z3,z4,z6]/(Bbar) is a FREE module of rank 6 over S = QQ[z2,z3,z4,z6] on 1, z1, ..., z1^5, and division in z1 by Bbar is exact over QQ with denominators only powers of that ONE rational (its primitive-integer representative has leading coefficient 2488320; the constant recorded here is the exact object's, and the two differ by the content this lane must not silently rescale away)",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "D1 EACH COLON TARGET REDUCES EXACTLY, BY ONE COMPLETE EXPANSION PER COLUMN.  For every n, D_n*col_n = q_n*Bbar + r_n with deg_z1(r_n) <= 5, verified coefficient-by-coefficient over QQ.  No Groebner basis, no prime and no reconstruction enters",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "D2 HENCE THE FIVE COLON QUESTIONS ARE UNCHANGED BUT SMALLER.  Bbar is a J50 generator, so D_n*col_n and r_n differ by a J50 element: `D_n in (J50 : col_n)` IF AND ONLY IF `r_n in J50`.  Each r_n is strictly smaller than its target and has z1-degree 5 rather than 43-49",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "D3 THE WHOLE RESIDUAL SHRINKS THE SAME WAY, BY ONE COMPLETE EXPANSION.  X = q_X*Bbar + rho with deg_z1(rho) <= 5, so X in J50 IFF rho in J50, and rho is STRICTLY smaller than X: 139616 terms against 175296, z1-degree 5 against 49",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "D4 THE COLUMN RESIDUES AND THE WHOLE RESIDUAL AGREE.  rho = sum_n r_n exactly, so the five-column split survives the reduction and the per-column obligations still sum to the single obligation",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "D5 THE REDUCTION DID NOT BUY THE SHRINK WITH COEFFICIENT HEIGHT.  The residual's height grows by less than 2 percent (2592 -> 2618 bits); an exact reduction that inflated the coefficients would be a worse object, not a better one",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "E1 THE 30 MODULE GENERATORS ARE EXACT AND CERTIFIED INDIVIDUALLY.  For each of the five non-Bbar generators g and each i <= 5, z1^i*g = w*Bbar + v with deg_z1(v) <= 5, by its own complete exact expansion (30 generators, 69472 terms total)",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "E2 THE RESIDUAL OBLIGATION IS A FOUR-VARIABLE MODULE MEMBERSHIP.  By C3 (freeness of rank 6 over S = QQ[z2,z3,z4,z6]) and E1 (the 30 certified generators of J50/(Bbar)), `rho in J50` IF AND ONLY IF the coordinate vector of rho lies in that S-submodule of S^6.  CHECKED HERE: the splitting of rho into its six coordinates is exact and term-complete.  Component sizes: [27668, 25874, 24013, 22356, 20646, 19059]",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "E3 NO COORDINATE OF THE RESTATED QUESTION IS EMPTY.  The target has a nonzero component in every one of the six free coordinates, so the restatement does not quietly discard part of the obligation.  NOT CLAIMED: that the submodule is proper -- that is equivalent to J50 being a proper ideal, which this lane does not decide (the modular basis of size 1271 is search data and does not exclude a rational unit certificate whose denominators the prime divides)",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "F1 NO COLON MEMBERSHIP IS CLAIMED.  This file proves a REDUCTION of the five colon questions and of X, not one of their answers.  Whether r_n or rho lies in J50 over QQ is exactly as open after this file as before it",
   "ok": true
  },
  {
   "check": "F2 NO ENTRY-T, LOCAL, AFF, C1, SUMMIT, H3 OR (75,125) CONSEQUENCE.  No emptiness of V(J50) cap D(h3), no h3^4 in J50, no manifest, DAG, status file or Lean artifact is touched",
